// RIGHT feedback (private message, specific, collaborative):
// "Hey, I noticed this method loads all orders into memory then filters.
// For large datasets that'll cause performance issues and potential OOM errors.
// Were you aware we can push the filter to the database layer?
// Here's how we could refactor it:"

public List<Order> findOrdersByCustomer(Long customerId) {
    // Query filters at database, returns only matching rows
    return orderRepository.findByCustomerId(customerId);
}

// Follow-up in message:
// "This reduces memory usage and is much faster because the database
// indexes customer_id. Want to pair on updating the other similar methods?
